# JVM tuning flags for the RecSys backend service.
#
# Memory model reference:
#   堆  (Heap)     – controlled by -Xms / -Xmx and G1 region/generation sizing
#   栈  (Stack)    – controlled by -Xss per-thread; reduced here because request
#                    handlers are shallow (no deep recursion in the inference path)
#   方法区/元空间   – controlled by -XX:MetaspaceSize / -XX:MaxMetaspaceSize;
#                    Spring Boot + ONNX Runtime load ~2 000 classes at startup,
#                    so we set a floor to avoid early metaspace GC pauses
#
# Usage:
#   java $(cat jvm.options) -jar recsys-api-*.jar
#   Or set JVM_OPTS="$(cat jvm.options)" and reference it in your start script.

# ── 堆 (Heap) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pre-allocate the full heap to avoid OS page-fault stalls under first load.
-Xms512m
-Xmx2g

# G1GC: best fit for this workload.
# Young gen handles high-throughput short-lived inference arrays (float[], Map).
# Old gen holds LocalEmbeddingCache (≤100 K float[128] vectors ≈ 50 MB) and
# TtlLruCache entries (≤10 K recommendation lists).
-XX:+UseG1GC

# 4 MB regions: float[128] = 512 bytes; arrays stay in regular regions,
# avoiding humongous allocation overhead for typical embedding sizes.
# Raise to 8 MB if you increase embedding dimensions beyond ~512 floats.
-XX:G1HeapRegionSize=4m

# Keep GC pauses under 100 ms on the inference hot path.
-XX:MaxGCPauseMillis=100

# Trigger a mixed collection (reclaims old-gen embedding slots) when old gen
# reaches 40% of heap, before it grows large enough to require a full GC.
-XX:InitiatingHeapOccupancyPercent=40

# Deduplicate identical String objects that arise from repeated feature keys
# (genre names, user-id strings, variant tags) interned across many requests.
-XX:+UseStringDeduplication

# ── 栈 (Stack) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default is 512 KB (Java 17). The serving path (HTTP → controller → ONNX → Redis)
# is shallow; 256 KB is sufficient and saves ~256 KB × thread-count of native memory.
-Xss256k

# ── 方法区 / 元空间 (Metaspace) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spring Boot 3 + ONNX Runtime + Jedis load roughly 8 000 – 10 000 classes.
# Setting the initial size prevents several rounds of metaspace GC at startup.
-XX:MetaspaceSize=128m

# Hard cap: avoids unbounded metaspace growth from dynamic proxies (CGLIB, Spring AOP).
# 256 MB is generous for this service; lower to 192 MB if memory is constrained.
-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=256m

# ── GC logging (observability) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Structured GC logs feed dashboards and diagnose pause regressions.
# Remove or redirect to /dev/null in environments where log volume is a concern.
-Xlog:gc*:file=gc.log:time,uptime,level,tags:filecount=5,filesize=20m

# ── Diagnostics ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Emit a heap dump on OOM rather than silently dying. Useful post-mortems when
# the embedding cache or recommendation cache grows unexpectedly.
-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:HeapDumpPath=heap-dump.hprof

# Print a summary of JVM flags actually in effect at startup (goes to stdout).
-XX:+PrintFlagsFinal
